For those of you who do not fully understand how NetHack is maintained:

The NetHack Development Team will issue, periodically, patchlevel revisions
of NetHack 3.1.  Those revisions will be in the form of context diffs, and
they will include both enhancements and bug fixes.  The patchlevel revisions
will presuppose that your code is synchronized with ours.  You are, of course,
free to modify your own code, but if you do, you should keep in mind that
you will encounter difficulties in applying the patchlevel revisions.

